a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T12:09:39-08:00","id":1193666,"title":"","content":"Definitely. That book is full of all kinds of fun surprises. The Mayor's &quot;origin story&quot; is among my favorites, together with Avarice and the mentions of the Blind Man and Thelema. Really helped to remind you that the greatest Night Horror that demons can stumble upon is things they don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T13:43:01-08:00","id":1193690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1193531#post1193531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Wednesday: &quot;Odin fights against God- why does it sounds so familiar?&quot;, also &quot;humanity has already tried to become god. No one liked the result&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, Odin was <i>not</i> an inspiration for Wednesday. Neither was Mr. Wednesday from American Gods.<br /> <br /> Wednesday's origins are fun, I'll tell it on the weekend*.<br /> <br /> *assuming I do not kill myself diving into a whiskey/Jessica Jones binge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T14:38:21-08:00","id":1193703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1193690#post1193690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funnily enough, Odin was <i>not</i> an inspiration for Wednesday. Neither was Mr. Wednesday from American Gods.<br /> <br /> Wednesday's origins are fun, I'll tell it on the weekend*.<br /> <br /> *assuming I do not kill myself diving into a whiskey/Jessica Jones binge.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here I thought that his raven form was a shout out for it. Just an happy coincidence, I assume :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T14:41:35-08:00","id":1193704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1193703#post1193703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here I thought that his raven form was a shout out for it. Just an happy coincidence, I assume :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing a bit of the story already, I will say this: Wednesday's animal Cover is an <i>extremely direct</i> reference to his narrative origins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T21:28:41-08:00","id":1193807,"title":"","content":"Well, Ms Morgue was thoroughly enjoyable to read. I kinda want to write some fiction with her as the protagonist now to see life from an angel's point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T21:52:39-08:00","id":1193811,"title":"","content":"Can I just say, I absolutely love Carta. She's no contest, my favorite thing in this book, and i love a lot in this book. It's just something about her hopelessness and determination and care that really strikes a cord in me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T21:56:35-08:00","id":1193812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1193811#post1193811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I just say, I absolutely love Carta. She's no contest, my favorite thing in this book, and i love a lot in this book. It's just something about her hopelessness and determination and care that really strikes a cord in me.</div> </div> </div> </div>She was one of my favorites, too. When I was reading everyone\u2019s drafts, I thought that she had a lot of potential. She will most likely appear in my games once I\u2019ve got a good place to put her in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T22:56:20-08:00","id":1193822,"title":"","content":"Oh as an aside (not too far in the book: most of my energy has been devoted to reading up Beast's PG) but in the intro...I got a bit of a laugh at the James Bond joke. Mostly because I just got done through a Bond-a-thon. Got a nice laugh from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T00:56:35-08:00","id":1193840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1193811#post1193811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I just say, I absolutely love Carta. She's no contest, my favorite thing in this book, and i love a lot in this book. It's just something about her hopelessness and determination and care that really strikes a cord in me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! She really spoke to me when I was writing her. I love her too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T04:09:39-08:00","id":1193873,"title":"","content":"So, one line thoughts about the Angel chapter-<br /> <br /> - Ataraxia: &quot;oh, she's looks nice. Kinda&quot;<br /> - Cheonsa: &quot;well, fuck&quot;<br /> - Jennifer: &quot;that's actually kinda cool!&quot;<br /> - Mdm. Wong: &quot;Oh, I feel sorry for her..&quot;<br /> - Mountain Maggie: &quot;I wonder what's that dead thin- OH MY GOD NO&quot;<br /> - Ms. Morgue: &quot;well, we're fucked&quot;<br /> - Ophelia: &quot;I think I'm scared now&quot;<br /> - Ricardo: &quot;Oh, I love him!&quot;<br /> - Summer: &quot;I... don't know how I feel?&quot;<br /> - Unwashed Isaac: &quot;Oh my god we are all doomed&quot; + &quot;THELEMA!!&quot; + &quot;ohhhhhh spoilers!&quot;<br /> <br /> All in all, I do really like how the angels are presented in the book, and how natural their Bans feel like when written into their character (the same goes for the glitches of demons in the previous chapter). I really liked the mention of Marco Singe and Avarice (which I now need to write down as a part of my &quot;Nine Parts Mechanism&quot;), and I loved the reference to Thelema, the Blind Men and Verney (not to mention the Contagion). I must wonder why would Morgue's fall would cause such a destruction, and I do hope that Wong would Fall. The Gardener is still my favorite in the chapter, I think.<br /> <br /> And as for Exiles-<br /> <br /> - Carta: &quot;poor thing&quot;, also &quot;what if.. ATLANTIS?!&quot;<br /> - Angel Maker: &quot;yeah, that's terrifying&quot;<br /> - Damocles: &quot;another poor Exile, in a fashion&quot;<br /> - Dosiel: &quot;yeah, that's scary&quot;<br /> - Lavadiel: &quot;yeah, that's a Night Horror&quot;<br /> - Lutzow: &quot;oh, my divine machineries...&quot;<br /> <br /> I must say that Dosiel reminds me of a concept I have for Raziel, the First Exile and keeper of the Machine's secrets, so I'll probably connect them together in some way (currently, I think of Raziel's very existence as being the said secret). Also, yeah, I do love Carta (like, I don;t know, everyone? She is a very lovable character), and while it was probably not the intention, with all the emphasis around crossovers I do imagine that the First City would be Atlantis. It's funny how Exiles pretty much divide between adorable and poor beings and terrifying monsters which scare the shit out of you. I'm kinda surprised there was no mention of Silvers in there, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T11:38:14-07:00","id":1194308,"title":"","content":"And here is the sum up of the last two chapters- first, Cryptids:<br /> <br /> - Alban: &quot;Oh, poor thing..&quot;<br /> - Asteroidea: &quot;Oh God why?&quot;<br /> - Beelzebub: &quot;well, that looks fun!&quot;<br /> - Black Mastiff: &quot;woofi.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;<br /> - Graveyard Bristle: &quot;Oh my fucking God Machine&quot; + &quot;who said that plants and zombies can't work together?&quot;<br /> - Hatchling: &quot;yet another thing you want to pet, but would probably get you killed&quot;<br /> - Oxblood Mold: &quot;I knew I hate molds for some reason..&quot;<br /> - Whispering Oak: &quot;scary tree is a scary tree&quot;<br /> <br /> I must say that a theme in that book is having just as many adorable antagonists as it has scary ones. The funny thing that among the chapter, Demon is the one which have the least sympathetic NPCs, and even there you have things like Mr. Martini or Mr. Void. Anyway, Beelzebub is my favorite antagonist in the section, as it reminds me of my concept for the Grigori (well, that and the Sanjha's special gadget). In my setting it would probably serve as a Cryptid which is being evolved into a full Grigori. Alban, on the other hand, is adorable- but I can't call it an antagonist. Its not its fault that people end up sacrificing their loved ones, and all it ones is a safe and loving home.. Also, mold vampires. Yikes.<br /> <br /> And finally- humans!<br /> <br /> - Bianca: &quot;you know what the God Machine says- you are fallen, but...&quot;<br /> - Brandon: &quot;well.. what the *** is going through the Machine's head?!&quot;<br /> - Carlota: &quot;and that's how dear old Gearhead fucks up&quot;<br /> - Donald: &quot;Not cool, G-M, not cool&quot;<br /> - Grace: &quot;Didn't I read something similar in the God Machine Anthologies?..&quot;<br /> - Liam: &quot;Well... that's interesting&quot;<br /> - Shauna: &quot;well, that's cool&quot;<br /> - Thousand Names of God: &quot;Wait- an whole bunch of DRIVERS?!&quot;<br /> <br /> So among of those, Liam is my favorite. Kinda reminds me of that Cuckoo mini template I once saw in the forums. Also, the Thousand Names are terrifying, especially since that chances are that what they are looking is, probably, the same &quot;pieces&quot; of Black Sun Map that the Driver from Slashers seeks after. Again, we have poor guys like Grace and Liam, and scar guys like the Thousand Names and Carlota. <br /> <br /> All in all-<br /> <br /> That was a very good book! From cool references like Thelema, Avaric and Neithian Architecture to plot hooks like Avarice, the Thousand Names and Brass, not to mention the cool and adorable NPCs such as Liam, the Gardener and Beelzebub, that book was indeed a cool one. While it felt a bit more &quot;friendly&quot; than how a Night Horror book usually is, it is still a book I'm glad I bought. Well done, to all writers!<br /> <br /> And as for my favorite character list-<br /> <br /> - The Gardener<br /> - Liam<br /> - Dosiel<br /> - Beelzebub<br /> - Brass<br /> <br /> And again, well done!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T16:45:26-07:00","id":1194390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1194308#post1194308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here is the sum up of the last two chapters- first, Cryptids:<br /> <br /> - Alban: &amp;quot;Oh, poor thing..&amp;quot;<br /> - Beelzebub: &amp;quot;well, that looks fun!&amp;quot;<br /> - Oxblood Mold: &amp;quot;I knew I hate molds for some reason..&amp;quot;<br /> - Whispering Oak: &amp;quot;scary tree is a scary tree&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I must say that a theme in that book is having just as many adorable antagonists as it has scary ones. The funny thing that among the chapter, Demon is the one which have the least sympathetic NPCs, and even there you have things like Mr. Martini or Mr. Void. Anyway, Beelzebub is my favorite antagonist in the section, as it reminds me of my concept for the Grigori (well, that and the Sanjha's special gadget). In my setting it would probably serve as a Cryptid which is being evolved into a full Grigori. Alban, on the other hand, is adorable- but I can't call it an antagonist. Its not its fault that people end up sacrificing their loved ones, and all it ones is a safe and loving home.. Also, mold vampires. Yikes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I\u2019m glad that you enjoyed my creations. I\u2019ve been worrying over whether I picked the right ones ever since I submitted them, so it\u2019s nice to see that they were well received. Now that they\u2019re out, if anyone has any questions or wishes to discuss my critters or what I was thinking when I came up with them, I no longer have any NDA ninjas preventing me from doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T09:06:05-07:00","id":1194550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1193873#post1193873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, one line thoughts about the Angel chapter-<br /> ...<br /> - Ms. Morgue: &quot;well, we're fucked&quot;<br /> - Ricardo: &quot;Oh, I love him!&quot;<br /> ...<br /> ... The Gardener is still my favorite in the chapter, I think.<br /> k.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I loved writing them both.<br /> <br /> My original thoughts on what happens with Ms. M's Fall were that she was willing to do anything to do more missions for the GM, including giving vital Infrastructure plans to Demons along with the tools to destroy it. The players' Ring then destroy the Infrastructure, and the city crumbles into chaos and riots without the Infrastructure. The God Machine does the biomechanical deity version of &quot;Oh, you are so fired,&quot; to Ms. Morgue; she Falls and happily becomes an Integrator mopping up corpses in the ruins, using her newfound ability to converse to brag about what she did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23990-gizmit","name":"Gizmit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23990_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T10:55:03-07:00","id":1194574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1194390#post1194390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you. I\u2019m glad that you enjoyed my creations. I\u2019ve been worrying over whether I picked the right ones ever since I submitted them, so it\u2019s nice to see that they were well received. Now that they\u2019re out, if anyone has any questions or wishes to discuss my critters or what I was thinking when I came up with them, I no longer have any NDA ninjas preventing me from doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must say that Beelzebub interests me the most, as I've had similar thought about &quot;demonic cryptids&quot; which eat demons for Cover- even though the execution was really different. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And on an unrelated note, I think I discovered a fun Easter Egg about Dosiel's name- while the word &quot;dos&quot; in hebrew doesn't really mean anything (well, it is a slang term for religious people, but nothing which really makes sense in context), the word &quot;sod&quot; actually means &quot;secret&quot;. More than that, the more archaic term for &quot;sod&quot; is &quot;raz&quot;- such as Raziel, the RL angel of secrets.<br /> <br /> So in fact, &quot;Dosiel&quot; kinda means &quot;the inversion of God's secret&quot;, which really fits his place in the setting- and yeah, I'm definitely going to tie him to my homebrew version of Raziel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T09:55:31-07:00","id":1195342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1194574#post1194574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that Beelzebub interests me the most, as I've had similar thought about &quot;demonic cryptids&quot; which eat demons for Cover- even though the execution was really different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I'm finally on an actual computer instead of my phone, I can finally address this.<br /> As you can no doubt imagine, I was quite excited when I was hired for this project. Before we even were given our assignments, I was brainstorming and pitching ideas for possible entries. It was while doing this that the first seeds of Beelzebub were formed. Since I didn't have my assignment yet, I wasn't restricting myself to the cryptids section, and I originally pitched him as an unnamed Analyst that had been created with a swarm-based form to research demons by infesting their demon's bodies. After his fall, he would have kept himself alive by claiming the bodies for his own and stealing their Covers. When we were asked which sections we'd like to write for, I put the cryptids as my first choice, mostly because I wanted to make certain that some cryptoflora made it in.<br /> When I was assigned four cryptids, I was delighted, and immediately began pitching ideas to John (my partner for that chapter). One of those initial ideas was a swarm of locusts that could take over or devour a demon's body, because the idea of a swarm of tiny creatures crawling between the spaces of a demon's form to control it or rip it apart for spare parts seemed like it would be horrific enough to make people's flesh crawl. Whatever I did with my critters, I always wanted to make certain that something about them screamed &quot;demonic&quot;, so that they would fit both with the Unchained and with more mainstream conceptions of the demonic. I had initially gone with locusts for that whole &quot;Biblical&quot; feel. I also considered whether I wanted to make it claim the identity of an entity from traditional demonology. It was about this time that I started thinking about the possibility of using biting flies rather than locusts, so that I could use the Beelzebub name, although I'd had other potential ones that I'd been considering, and those would have probably left them as locusts if I'd chosen one of those names instead. I decided upon the flies in the end for a couple reasons. The first is that it separated my critter further from the locust Hosts in Werewolf: The Forsaken, which had been a bit of a concern. The second and more important reason was that I'd learned about cerebral myiasis, and the idea of brain maggots making people into temporary &quot;Sleeper agents&quot; for the swarm was just too horrific not to use. The fact that Beelzebub was the most famous demon name I was considering was just icing on the cake.<br /> So that's how Beelzebub came to be one of my critters for Enemy Action. I could go on a bit about what I was thinking while writing him, but I might have rambled on more than was desired already, so I'll leave that for if there's any interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:23:12-07:00","id":1195497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1195342#post1195342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that I'm finally on an actual computer instead of my phone, I can finally address this.<br /> As you can no doubt imagine, I was quite excited when I was hired for this project. Before we even were given our assignments, I was brainstorming and pitching ideas for possible entries. It was while doing this that the first seeds of Beelzebub were formed. Since I didn't have my assignment yet, I wasn't restricting myself to the cryptids section, and I originally pitched him as an unnamed Analyst that had been created with a swarm-based form to research demons by infesting their demon's bodies. After his fall, he would have kept himself alive by claiming the bodies for his own and stealing their Covers. When we were asked which sections we'd like to write for, I put the cryptids as my first choice, mostly because I wanted to make certain that some cryptoflora made it in.<br /> When I was assigned four cryptids, I was delighted, and immediately began pitching ideas to John (my partner for that chapter). One of those initial ideas was a swarm of locusts that could take over or devour a demon's body, because the idea of a swarm of tiny creatures crawling between the spaces of a demon's form to control it or rip it apart for spare parts seemed like it would be horrific enough to make people's flesh crawl. Whatever I did with my critters, I always wanted to make certain that something about them screamed &amp;quot;demonic&amp;quot;, so that they would fit both with the Unchained and with more mainstream conceptions of the demonic. I had initially gone with locusts for that whole &amp;quot;Biblical&amp;quot; feel. I also considered whether I wanted to make it claim the identity of an entity from traditional demonology. It was about this time that I started thinking about the possibility of using biting flies rather than locusts, so that I could use the Beelzebub name, although I'd had other potential ones that I'd been considering, and those would have probably left them as locusts if I'd chosen one of those names instead. I decided upon the flies in the end for a couple reasons. The first is that it separated my critter further from the locust Hosts in Werewolf: The Forsaken, which had been a bit of a concern. The second and more important reason was that I'd learned about cerebral myiasis, and the idea of brain maggots making people into temporary &amp;quot;Sleeper agents&amp;quot; for the swarm was just too horrific not to use. The fact that Beelzebub was the most famous demon name I was considering was just icing on the cake.<br /> So that's how Beelzebub came to be one of my critters for Enemy Action. I could go on a bit about what I was thinking while writing him, but I might have rambled on more than was desired already, so I'll leave that for if there's any interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abaddon, angel of the abyss and prince of locusts, whines at a chance lost to appear in human culture. <br /> <br /> Just kidding- great work you\u2019ve done there. I now know what entry to pay attention to when I finally pick up the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T16:09:56-07:00","id":1195520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1195497#post1195497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Abaddon, angel of the abyss and prince of locusts, whines at a chance lost to appear in human culture. <br /> <br /> Just kidding- great work you\u2019ve done there. I now know what entry to pay attention to when I finally pick up the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m glad that you like where I went with the idea, and I\u2019m flattered that you\u2019re looking forward to it. That said, I think that you\u2019ll find all the entries in the book to be worthy of attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T19:41:01-07:00","id":1195586,"title":"","content":"Okay, I like Ophelia Adder. She definitely gets the idea across that sometimes even angels can be on the same side as the Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T14:02:39-07:00","id":1195837,"title":"","content":"Alban is very interesting. Reminds me a lot of the Azazel.I could easily see dropping the Judus Goat into a mortals, Second Sight, or Mage game and watching the Time/Space havoc fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:42:36-07:00","id":1195896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1195837#post1195837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alban is very interesting. Reminds me a lot of the Azazel.I could easily see dropping the Judus Goat into a mortals, Second Sight, or Mage game and watching the Time/Space havoc fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m glad you found Alban interesting. He was one of the ones I was most worried about being disliked, given that he is more of a trouble magnet than an active threat to the Unchained. I had not considered any similarities to Azazel when I was writing him. I think mages would be the best suited to deal with Alban permanently, but it could be fun in the others, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T16:41:11-07:00","id":1196280,"title":"","content":"The suicide counselor angel kind of hit home for me. Not sure why. Really well written, but it left me feeling in a pretty dark place. I could easily write a scenario around her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T16:45:22-07:00","id":1196283,"title":"","content":"Just coming in to say that, though my PDF's budget went elsewhere, from what I'm reading the book will be on my list of things to order when the Print-On-Demand option appears.<br /> <br /> I know it's not much when it comes to praise, but reading the impressions and comments you all wrote here after the book came out convinced me quite easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-16-2018, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T04:39:47-07:00","id":1196447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1196283#post1196283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just coming in to say that, though my PDF's budget went elsewhere, from what I'm reading the book will be on my list of things to order when the Print-On-Demand option appears.<br /> <br /> I know it's not much when it comes to praise, but reading the impressions and comments you all wrote here after the book came out convinced me quite easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. I haven't the money at the moment to get a hold of it, but I will when I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T08:07:05-07:00","id":1196488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1195896#post1195896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m glad you found Alban interesting. He was one of the ones I was most worried about being disliked, given that he is more of a trouble magnet than an active threat to the Unchained. I had not considered any similarities to Azazel when I was writing him. I think mages would be the best suited to deal with Alban permanently, but it could be fun in the others, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, all four of your cryptids were fun and interesting to read. I was very happy to see cryptoflora and cryptofungi make their way in to the book as well!<br /> <br /> Just the section on cults to go and I'm done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T12:59:51-07:00","id":1196571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1196488#post1196488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, all four of your cryptids were fun and interesting to read. I was very happy to see cryptoflora and cryptofungi make their way in to the book as well!<br /> <br /> Just the section on cults to go and I'm done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m glad that you enjoyed them. Getting cryptoflora into the book was one of my top priorities when I started brainstorming ideas, as I felt like they had a lot of unexplored potential. I was pleased when Matt approved the first four ideas I submitted for the cryptids. I only wish that there\u2019d also been room in the book for some of the second batch of ideas I\u2019d been preparing to send.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T13:41:39-07:00","id":1196585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1196571#post1196571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m glad that you enjoyed them. Getting cryptoflora into the book was one of my top priorities when I started brainstorming ideas, as I felt like they had a lot of unexplored potential. I was pleased when Matt approved the first four ideas I submitted for the cryptids. I only wish that there\u2019d also been room in the book for some of the second batch of ideas I\u2019d been preparing to send.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blog post? Thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T15:16:16-07:00","id":1196620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1196283#post1196283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just coming in to say that, though my PDF's budget went elsewhere, from what I'm reading the book will be on my list of things to order when the Print-On-Demand option appears.<br /> <br /> I know it's not much when it comes to praise, but reading the impressions and comments you all wrote here after the book came out convinced me quite easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really should! It is excellent!<br /> <br /> So the One Thousand Names are pretty cool. Seems like a mix of Gnosticism, Sufism, and Freemasonry, then it veers hard left into Abstergo territory. If I wanted to recreate Assassin's Creed in CofD so I could use multiple Dark Eras in one contemporary chronicle, these would be the people I'd give the Animus to!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T23:22:56-07:00","id":1196729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1196585#post1196585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blog post? Thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, maybe I will. I do have one of them that\u2019s about half written already, as at one point there was a chance that I would have been replacing Whispering Oak. I guess I could finish her up and post her as an unofficial tie-in. I think I have a couple of the others started as well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T07:23:36-07:00","id":1197178,"title":"","content":"Is it just me, or is Cheosa a bit light for a rank 4 Angel with only 9 dots among power and resistance. Sure I get she can pump up her stats with essence and has powers related to emotional influence, plus Armor 3, but shouldn't her stats be higher or would that make her (it?) Too tough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T07:25:16-07:00","id":1197179,"title":"","content":"Now this is rather late, but I have to say that there are two Angels, or rather an Angel and an Exile I really, really like. Ophelia Adder and Damocles. The former being because I really enjoy the AI angle and the God-Machine\u2019s reaction to it- as well as Ophelia herself being a very interesting antagonist. As someone who loves Demon for its techgnostic theme, this really helps play up the technological aspect of Demon.<br /> <br /> ... and since I have a bit of a love for the fan game Sovereign.. my mind races with crossover potential.<br /> <br /> As for Damocles, it\u2019s not so much the character himself that interests me, though he is a delightfully hands on Analyst ( which is apparently the teams favorite Incarnation, seeing how nearly a third of the demon/angel antagonists are Analysts- rare and mysterious my ass xD ) but the Legacy he represents- the Damocles Project. The idea of the God-Machine actively trying to make an \u201cultimate \u201c Destroyer is fascinating and makes me wonder if Damocles himself still will have a part to play in this uncharacteristically ambitious project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T10:40:56-07:00","id":1197257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1197179#post1197179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Damocles, it\u2019s not so much the character himself that interests me, though he is a delightfully hands on Analyst ( which is apparently the teams favorite Incarnation, seeing how nearly a third of the demon/angel antagonists are Analysts- rare and mysterious my ass xD ).</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, I also felt the bit of &quot;Analyst Overload&quot;- but there are exactly two demons for each Incarnation, among the angels only the Gardener is called to be Analysts (the others are mostly Destroyers, I think- it is usually not stated from what I see) and 1 to 2 Exiles (I'm not sure if Dosiel is an Analyst- he does feels so, but it is not stated)., so I think there is no &quot;Analyst population explosion&quot; or something like that :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T11:08:52-07:00","id":1197269,"title":"","content":"Also adding on Lost Light's Statement, If i remember correctly, Damocles is explicitly a psychopomp, not an analyst","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T12:14:13-07:00","id":1197287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1197269#post1197269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also adding on Lost Light's Statement, If i remember correctly, Damocles is explicitly a psychopomp, not an analyst</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, he is specifically said to be an Analyst who was designed for the purpose of studying and improving upon firearms and other Weaponry- guns just happened to be where his main interest lay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T15:20:32-07:00","id":1197351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1197287#post1197287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, he is specifically said to be an Analyst who was designed for the purpose of studying and improving upon firearms and other Weaponry- guns just happened to be where his main interest lay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Huh. then i guess 2-3 Exiles are Analysts then (As Carta is also 100% an Analysts)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T17:29:17-07:00","id":1198464,"title":"","content":"Well, here's the thing about Analysts, as is noted in <b>Demon: Interface</b> (and the ST Guide):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: Interface, p. 58</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Analyst angels are perhaps the most common of the God-Machine\u2019s servants...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that when we say they're rare, we mean it's rare for them to be demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 03-23-2018, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T02:31:12-07:00","id":1198986,"title":"","content":"So what can we glean from Unwashed Isaac about the Contagion Chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T23:27:08-07:00","id":1201156,"title":"","content":"Oh my gosh, I love Mage and all but NOTHING gets the storyhooks nearly as well as Demon! From Dark Eras to any Demon book, the whole cosmos comes rolling together in the most frustratingly mysterious and mesmerizing ways!<br /> <br /> Okay, can someone PLEASE help me with who the Blind and Angry Man(s) are? Just tell me what books I need and where to read about them, or if that's hard then a little bit of info.<br /> <br /> Cuz as soon as the book paired The Old Man near two other mysterious figures and hinted that they somehow give Isaac pause I just BURNED with curiosity. I do not know who the Blind Man is or who the Angry Man is but I definitely know who the Old Man is and that's one of my favorite mythical CofD figures~<br /> <br /> Also I'm with Stannis. I've heard a rumor about something called the Contagion Chronicle but I'm nooot familiar with what that is at all D: help a girl out<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T23:35:03-07:00","id":1201161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1201156#post1201156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I'm with Stannis. I've heard a rumor about something called the Contagion Chronicle but I'm nooot familiar with what that is at all D: help a girl out</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a rumor. It's an official upcoming product.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book\">Thread here</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T23:47:55-07:00","id":1201167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1201156#post1201156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my gosh, I love Mage and all but NOTHING gets the storyhooks nearly as well as Demon! From Dark Eras to any Demon book, the whole cosmos comes rolling together in the most frustratingly mysterious and mesmerizing ways!<br /> <br /> Okay, can someone PLEASE help me with who the Blind and Angry Man(s) are? Just tell me what books I need and where to read about them, or if that's hard then a little bit of info.<br /> <br /> Cuz as soon as the book paired The Old Man near two other mysterious figures and hinted that they somehow give Isaac pause I just BURNED with curiosity. I do not know who the Blind Man is or who the Angry Man is but I definitely know who the Old Man is and that's one of my favorite mythical CofD figures~<br /> <br /> Also I'm with Stannis. I've heard a rumor about something called the Contagion Chronicle but I'm nooot familiar with what that is at all D: help a girl out</div> </div> </div> </div>The Blind Man can be found in Beast's Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes; he's one of the Insatiable, predators of the Begotten who claim kinship with them... something the Beasts don't reciprocate.<br /> <br /> The Angry Man? Verney from the Promethean 1e core, who claims to be Frankenstein's original monster.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T00:05:02-07:00","id":1201170,"title":"","content":"Thank you all! What a rabbit-hole I've found myself in. I think I read about Verney already, but I don't have Beast's Night Horrors. Thanks! Will look into this :3 ((unrelated note, maybe not discussion worthy since out of topic, but, I'm thinking the contagion sounds like the abyssal spin on divine fire! Or just my interest in China Meville's concept of &quot;torque&quot; ;3 ))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T19:23:05-07:00","id":1205054,"title":"","content":"Heeey looks the PoD for this bad boy will be ready to go on Wednesday!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T07:09:22-07:00","id":1206012,"title":"","content":"It is indeed, with errata incorporated! Here you go: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/236133/Night-Horrors-Enemy-Action?affiliate_id=182989\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...iate_id=182989</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:45:59-07:00","id":1211941,"title":"","content":"Should get my copy by tomorow. I haven't bought the PDF, so it's gonna be all new for me. But I do expect great things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 04-26-2018, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T13:48:12-07:00","id":1211961,"title":"","content":"Got mine yesterday. The circle is complete. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T06:25:55-07:00","id":1213401,"title":"","content":"Alright, now that I have the book within my hands, I can say for certain it's a good one. One of the most solid of the Night Horrors series, and that's meant as a high compliment. Skimmed through it all and read Cryptids and Angels (what can I say, being a modular book I go first to what I enjoy more), and liked most of what I've seen.<br /> <br /> Some I actually loved more than others, like Beelzebub (which is a great antagonist) and Alban (which I want to hug) and Ophelia Adder and Unwashed Isaac, but overall the books filled with cool content and lot of hooks and ideas, both explicit and implied.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T13:09:48-07:00","id":1213513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1213401#post1213401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, now that I have the book within my hands, I can say for certain it's a good one. One of the most solid of the Night Horrors series, and that's meant as a high compliment. Skimmed through it all and read Cryptids and Angels (what can I say, being a modular book I go first to what I enjoy more), and liked most of what I've seen.<br /> <br /> Some I actually loved more than others, like Beelzebub (which is a great antagonist) and Alban (which I want to hug) and Ophelia Adder and Unwashed Isaac, but overall the books filled with cool content and lot of hooks and ideas, both explicit and implied.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m glad that you liked Beelzebub and Alban. I was very proud of both of those. On the subject of Alban, now that a lot of people have had the chance to read the book, I can speak a little bit about what I was thinking when writing him. Specifically, I\u2019m going to answer the question that everyone has been desperately trying to figure out (by which, of course, I mean that there may have been a person who vaguely wondered about it in passing and then didn\u2019t think of it ever again). So, why exactly did I decide to give the goat purple eyes? Despite what most people would probably assume, it wasn\u2019t just random weirdness. It was, in fact, a small tribute to a dear friend of mine that passed away a couple years ago. Blind Eric was a pretty cool guy. I\u2019ve got tons of stories about him, but rather than completely derailing the thread, I\u2019ll just say that he was knife collecting, Odin worshiping blind man with a twisted sense of humor and a love of role playing games and martial arts. Eric had two glass eyes, and he wasn\u2019t opposed to having a little fun with them at other people\u2019s expense. He sometimes mentioned that he wished he could afford to purchase some high end, custom glass eyes, and one of his dream pairs would be a set of purple goat\u2019s eyes. When I started writing Alban, I decided very early on that I would give the poor creature the eyes that Eric always wanted, as a small nod to my departed friend. And now you all know the answer to the question nobody asked, but that I wanted to answer anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T20:52:56-08:00","id":1282781,"title":"","content":"So I have the writing in me, but I need a break, so it occurred to me I never told the story of Wednesday. So, let's do that.<br /> <br /> Actually, no, first, context on why Wednesday is in Enemy Action.<br /> <br /> So back when the bids for who got what were going on, my original bid was for a demon and a stigmatic. The Demon was always going to be Sanjha, as I've been wanting to get a rakshasa(or rakshasi, as it turned out being) in Descent for forever and a day, and the stigmatic was going to be someone cribbing on the magical girl aesthetic because I have also been wanting to get a magical girl into Chronicles forever and a Stigmatic has actually always been my preferred take on it. Sanjha was very different in the original thought process, more directly tackling a Hindu interpretation of Descent's lore, having her directly confront the God-Machine as the incarnation of the Samsara and employing her Covers as a means of hacking the wheel of incarnation to directly confront reality on multiple layers in pursuit of Nirvana for herself and a select few.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, I got thwarted by the most mundane of vectors: When I replied to the request for what I was bidding on, I replied to a fellow author instead of doing Reply All to stake my claim, and so at the end of the day, I got two demons instead. And I, for a brief bit, had no idea who the second demon was going to be....until the obvious stared me in the face. I had <i>played</i> the character that deserved to be the second demon.<br /> <br /> Which is funny, because Wednesday was not a demon when I started playing him. He was a bird.<br /> <br /> Back in the first year of attending BYU-I, I had been part of a Mage the Ascension game, with the party being this small cadre of Mages who were also really just drug addicts and dealers. In that game, we had the Ecstatic, Aaron Black, drug dealer and teacher of enlightenment who aspired for the elevation of humanity on the whole, Lydia Megan [last name here](called Megan 2), who was a newly Awakened mage taking lessons from Aaron and generally kind of a clean kid, and finally the Verbana Witch Megan Calloway(called Megan 1), a heroin addict and homeless woman whose mentor-and-only-real-father-figure was mysteriously killed. Matt, the guy who played Megan, wanted to have a Familiar, but was having trouble divvying up the points for his Spheres in a way that satisfied him and got it. So, instead, Megan inherited the familiar, a raven, from her mentor Gregory Calloway.<br /> <br /> And because that sounded cooler and weirder than the paladin I was planning on, I decided I was going to play that familiar.<br /> <br /> In case you ever caught one of the light arguments I've had about the playability of familiars in Mage, now you know why. I fleshed out the raven by saying that it was inhabited by a time spirit called Twisted-Hours-from-Broken-Seconds, the result of a drug trip meeting an Awakening, and proposed the name Wednesday because I had gotten Matt to read American Gods recently and liked it better than Huginn or Muninn. I also gave the bird Amnesia and Dark Fate, because I didn't want to think too hard about what led Twist to this place.<br /> <br /> The first half of the game was basically us dicking around, selling drugs, looking for a Node of our own, occasionally running foul of the the mobs in Seattle, resolving tensions with werewolves who are responding to the growth a thousand year old tree in five years, stuff like that. It was by and large just a group of broken people hanging out and becoming a surrogate little family as they tried and failed at a lot of random things. We snuck into a Mormon temple and had to help Megan 2 out because her shyness kept her from saying no to these weirdos who somehow had a Node, we scared off a heavy addict, had an awkward dinner party with a recovering addict, we botched a drug deal, Me and Aaron got high to discover some secrets and then flooded the house because we thought it was one fire, I had legitimate cause to say &quot;I am the terror that flaps in the night!&quot; once and discovered pork rinds, stuff like that. It was fun shenanigans. <br /> <br /> That all started to change when circumstances forced us to investigate the Calloway Manor. Greg's body was still in the main entry way.<br /> <br /> It turns out a lot of things that were starting to happen, that were changing, that were moving in response to something, were rooted in Greg's murder, and the ambition behind it. We soon discovered there was a demon who was moving around, building a base of power and arranging things in anticipation of a celestial convergence that was going to change the game for a lot of people-in other games, it let the Order of Hermes wage unholy war with the vampires of Los Angeles and kick off a new mage/vampire war, and it also allowed for a mass resurrection in New York- and that Gregory Calloway had helped the demon to figure out what to do with it.<br /> <br /> On my own side of things, I learned from the god of the forest that my character was fundamentally broken, missing parts of himself. In fact, I think that was the final straw that led us to the Manor-I went in before anyone else. Upon discovering the shadow man who had killed Greg, I started tracking him down, and I found him. I found the demon named Cacus, and he had found me. I found him because I was time.<br /> <br /> He found me because he had other parts of me, and he gave them back to me. I became whole in a way I didn't know was missing. Not completely whole-but enough to know how much more I was broken.<br /> <br /> Turns out, Wednesday wasn't a spirit, but a demon-a Fiend named Zrvaniel, who was one of a few who had managed to find a way out of the Abyss really early on and also managed to avoid becoming Earthbound, and had incarnated over the ages as all manner of things, including Persian Gods and Roman Commanders, Greek Monsters and Norse Sages-and more. Zrvaniel had a problem, though, where the War in Heaven had left him fragile-death caused his fragmented essence to scatter, and time was mostly needed for him to come back together. In the meantime, he mostly believed that he was whatever he was inhabiting at the time. Gregory Calloway had bound him as a familiar, and because of the way bonds work, the death of Greg had also fragmented Zrvaniel, and should anything happen to Megan now, Zrvan would also scatter.<br /> <br /> And it was Wednesday who had come up with the plan to defeat God-using the psychic guidance and pressure of an elder demon, Wednesday, Cacus, and Nothiel(who was the recovering addict, actually) would elevate humanity into Awakening, and continue to nurture them until they could collectively overthrow the Demon, at which point, with the alliance of the Fallen to them, they could overcome God. Cacus saw them as generals over humanity even in their Awakened state, Wednesday felt they were more shepherds and closer in alliance than that-but either way, they all were determined to pit the whole of Humanity Awakened against God and <i>win</i>.<br /> <br /> This....was a problem. Megan 1 was vehemently against Cacus for killing Greg, and determined to ruin all his efforts, Megan 2 in the meanwhile had been raised Christian and had trouble trusting that anything coming from a demon was good. On the opposite side, it was <i>my</i> plan, one I committed to because, like the other demons in the war, I loved humanity and desire to see their inheritance come to pass. Meanwhile, Aaron Black was infiltrating the cult of Nothiel, and was mostly on board with the Awakening of all mankind since that was his MO anyways, though he was skeptical.<br /> <br /> It was a rough time. Megan 1 nearly killed me with a book, one time we thought Aaron was being a traitor so we tortured him by popping limbs out of sockets until he revealed he was about to tell us all the truth anyways, eventually a demonologist yanked me together into a whole being and Megan bound me with my name, I took posession of a human, we discovered the randomly growing tree was the earth's response to the ritual coming up, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> The family basically ended.<br /> <br /> In the end, we had to make decisions. Wednesday decided to put faith in humanity by trusting Megan to allow the ritual to happen, but turned on his partner since the dawn of time and murdered him for her revenge in order to try and make that happen. Aaron went full on into the cult and committed to the ritual. The Megans teamed up with Mormon Celestial Choristers and wiped out Ritual spot one, and then basically shot the essence of the tree into the ritual, shattering the elder demon and killing all but Aaron, who became a host for a shard of the elder, but at the cost of Megan 1 falling into a coma. Wednesday would have committed suicide and abided in the Abyss until the end of days, except that the spell that cancelled out the ritual shatter him again, leaving him as a confused young man, who Megan 2 decided to take care of and watch. Aaron said goodbye to Megan in her coma, and then left to wander the earth, searching for the elder demon's shards.<br /> <br /> By the way, this in a world where our other games are following the journey of the Antichrist and leading to inevitable End of the World. We recommitted to finishing the Desdemona Chronicle this year, in fact.<br /> <br /> Wednesday is one my best characters, and his humanist-driven probably-world-ending ambition was basically too good to pass up for in Enemy Action, someone whose motivations and goals are all too twisty to neatly name him villain and protagonist, and therefore someone who fit the bill of book perfectly. His issue with memory and the way that affected his relationship to humanity was also a unique vector that I thought would make him different from the others-in the end, I never could get that to quite look like I wanted it to, since I also wanted to provide player tools with my characters and the two desires clashed, but I did what I could. He's also an important character for me personally, because it was playing as him that solidified the friendships with the people I'm living with even now.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. I admit, he might not be the most interesting of the demons in Enemy Action (there are a lot of cool characters in there, no lie), but once I got that pitch, I think you can see why I had to put him in. Hope you all can find as good a use for him in your games as he ended up serving in our best game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T23:00:38-08:00","id":1282795,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> That is a seriously cool origin, and it goes a ways to elaborate on Wednesday's personality and the dangers therein. I'm presuming that his alternate Covers are further references to this game - highly approve of that. Thanks for sharing it with us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T01:39:05-08:00","id":1282812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1192684-night-horrors-enemy-action-on-dtrpg?p=1282795#post1282795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> That is a seriously cool origin, and it goes a ways to elaborate on Wednesday's personality and the dangers therein. I'm presuming that his alternate Covers are further references to this game - highly approve of that. Thanks for sharing it with us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the only direct reference is the raven. Alexander Wayfarer ties into how the capabilities of Mages heavily informs the theory and basis he works from (While the rules kept me from making a full crossover villain, it has always been my intent that Wednesday be a character who can act as a villain in a lot of the other gamelines), and while Wendy was the familiar's nickname, Wendy Odile Elian was my initial answer to how Wednesday would operate in the world of Descent. At the end of the Mage game, he had possessed a young man with black hair, and some of that got gender swapped into Wendy.<br /> <br /> THAT SAID, you'll note that the third major hook is basically me trying to jam in as much of the original story in as possible, and if you want me to provide a definitive answer for how old Wednesday is in Descent, consider how he might interact with the Sundering, or what role he had in the First Legion if you take that as canon.<br /> <br /> And above all else, it's important to note: Wednesday <i>could have won that game</i>. While definitely fraught with problems following the initial success, both of the storytellers handling that individual game(BRjedi, for those who remember him), and the Desdemona Chronicle(Matt, not one y'all know) affirmed that Wednesday could have taken down God with the results, with the major remaining question being how much of the world would be left. Hell, once he gets a proper look at the board with Dessie and the changed world, he still might be able to win against God (Matt once noted that the option I offered of Wednesday restructuring the Old World into the Chronicles World wasn't outside the realm of possibility). In Descent terms, he is a full Arcane Physicist, and while he may need stars in alignment to succeed, this is a Demon who, along with Cacus and Nothiel(Who I'll chat about more sometime), had to be stopped by<i> Hercules</i>(Assume the story of Cacus as we know it to be severely truncated). While Wednesday can, and should, play part in local, regional, and global tiers, the threat of his ambitions are always Cosmic.<br /> <br /> Wednesday's child is full of woe indeed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, again, it can't be overemphasized-his ability to both forget and dive deep into living his Covers is always a big part of what forms his convictions. Wednesday is an object lesson in how the distance and isolation of the Unchained(and the Fallen) is as much a blessing as it is it's own torment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-26-2019, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}